From 224dd964d791fb3ba3a179394df2edb2abfdf294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:42:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/33] Plugins: a text size for each plugin

A plugin's text could be as large as it made it, larger than the
meter's. Two buttons in the dock's panel bar and in a plugin's own
window (smaller, larger) set its text size: 60% to 125% in seven steps,
kept for each plugin, the same in the dock and in its own window. The
plugin's frame is laid out larger by as much as it is scaled down, so
it fills its place and has more room for its content; a height it asks
the window to fit to (an alert) is scaled with it. A transform rather
than zoom: WebKitGTK applies a frame's zoom only as its page loads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RBQati3x8VviBbpY9juEWf
